      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "In rats, compound 3a had a brain-to-plasma unbound concentration ratio of ~0.1 in the FIRF assay, reported as impaired CNS penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple direct systemic pharmacokinetic studies in rats and other species demonstrate meaningful CNS access, with brain:plasma ratios from 0.14 to 3.4 and positive PET/uptake evidence. One low unbound ratio is an outlier and does not override the consistent positive in-vivo record.",
